{"about_the_game":"<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>What is this?</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This VR game is a time machine, but you don't get to choose where you go. When you pull the lever it takes you somewhere random.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You get a date telling you where you are in time and the doors open. There's no way of predicting where you'll end up. You can't leave the time machine -  you can stick your head out, but be warned sometimes you might not want to.  </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Where do I go?</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You might end up somewhere significant or you might end up somewhere totally ordinary.  </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If you don't like where you are then you pull the lever again. </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Controls</strong> </h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game takes place in a single 2x3m room. You can use teleport and smooth locomotion to move around in the space if you would like to play sitting down. Its best played roomscale. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2707810/extras/2f5324375d47244fa87714892f5ff546.poster.avif?t=1765154374\" width=616 height=180 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2707810/extras/2f5324375d47244fa87714892f5ff546.webm?t=1765154374\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2707810/extras/2f5324375d47244fa87714892f5ff546.mp4?t=1765154374\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Have fun! </p>","achievements":{"highlighted":[{"name":"Everywhere","path":"https://cdn.akamai.steamstatic.com/steamcommunity/public/images/apps/2707810/b13477fdeb443198f780bd52b86d89c66bad6e0c.jpg"},{"name":"Tic Tac?","path":"https://cdn.akamai.steamstatic.com/steamcommunity/public/images/apps/2707810/ada6806432f2cc2b09f4dab24c6c853e27b71888.jpg"},{"name":"Neo and Jerry","path":"https://cdn.akamai.steamstatic.com/steamcommunity/public/images/apps/2707810/a00d19754242ab68376e47ff31633a813376b6d8.jpg"},{"name":" Simulacra and Simulation","path":"https://cdn.akamai.steamstatic.com/steamcommunity/public/images/apps/2707810/c20fa9b7b34c088491a21b1cfd9ca4f4c7d785cc.jpg"},{"name":"Reunification","path":"https://cdn.akamai.steamstatic.com/steamcommunity/public/images/apps/2707810/ada21c256d6ea2d52b887d7beb8aab5b6e5eb674.jpg"},{"name":"High Score!","path":"https://cdn.akamai.steamstatic.com/steamcommunity/public/images/apps/2707810/111f2aa98681029ca72328cfa485cc6963186989.jpg"}],"total":6},"background":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/2707810?t=1765154374","background_raw":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2707810/0054aac222e4321571682356ab6b0a98cc7400da/page_bg_raw.jpg?t=1765154374","capsule_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2707810/0c31ab4887b5734dd984d6fb035dc5dd46ef4d07/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1765154374","capsule_imagev5":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2707810/0c31ab4887b5734dd984d6fb035dc5dd46ef4d07/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1765154374","categories":[{"description":"Single-player","id":2},{"description":"Steam Achievements","id":22},{"description":"Tracked Controller Support","id":52},{"description":"VR Only","id":54},{"description":"Camera Comfort","id":67},{"description":"Playable without Timed Input","id":74},{"description":"Stereo Sound","id":69},{"description":"Surround Sound","id":70},{"description":"Family Sharing","id":62}],"content_descriptors":{"ids":[5],"notes":"The Time Machine presents dioramas of real historical settings. There is no gore, violence, or graphic content, but some locations depict politically or socially contentious moments from history."},"detailed_description":"<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>What is this?</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This VR game is a time machine, but you don't get to choose where you go. When you pull the lever it takes you somewhere random.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You get a date telling you where you are in time and the doors open. There's no way of predicting where you'll end up. You can't leave the time machine -  you can stick your head out, but be warned sometimes you might not want to.  </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Where do I go?</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You might end up somewhere significant or you might end up somewhere totally ordinary.  </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If you don't like where you are then you pull the lever again. </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Controls</strong> </h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game takes place in a single 2x3m room. You can use teleport and smooth locomotion to move around in the space if you would like to play sitting down. Its best played roomscale. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2707810/extras/2f5324375d47244fa87714892f5ff546.poster.avif?t=1765154374\" width=616 height=180 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2707810/extras/2f5324375d47244fa87714892f5ff546.webm?t=1765154374\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2707810/extras/2f5324375d47244fa87714892f5ff546.mp4?t=1765154374\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_p